course: dictionary
lesson: 6444
title: Nameless and what it hides
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Nameless means having no name, or having a name that nobody knows. «The nameless stranger walked into the village.» We do not know who he is, so we cannot call him by a name. The clue is the word name hidden inside it.
explain: Sometimes a name is kept secret on purpose. «Who shall remain nameless» is a joke way of saying you will not say someone's name. In the news, «A royal source says» is a nameless claim. We cannot tell who the source is, so we cannot check if the claim is right, wrong or made up.
explain: A nameless feeling is one that is too strange or strong to describe. «She felt a nameless dread as the lights went out.» She had a scary feeling but could not put it into words. Check any meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does the sentence still make sense?
fact: Nameless means having no name, or whose name is not known.
fact: Nameless can also mean whose name is kept secret on purpose.
fact: «A nameless fear» is a feeling that is too strange or strong to describe.
fact: «Nameless soldiers» are people in history whose names were lost.
fact: In the news, «unnamed» means much the same as nameless.
exercise: «The nameless stranger walked into the village.» What does nameless mean here? | Very famous and well known | Happy and loud | Wearing a name badge | *Having no name that anyone knows
exercise: Ella says, «Who shall remain nameless has been sent a letter.» What does the phrase mean? | The person has no name at all in the world | The person is very rude | The name is too long to say | *Not saying the name on purpose
exercise: «She felt a nameless dread as the lights went out.» What does nameless suggest? | *A fear too strange and strong to describe | A happy surprise | A name she had forgotten | Cold hands
test: «A royal source says the king is ill.» Why might a careful reader doubt this claim? | Because kings are never ill | Because source is a long word | Because the sentence is too long | *The person saying it is nameless, so we cannot check who they are
test: «The nameless workers built the bridge, but their names were lost.» Copy the word that means having no known name. | names | bridge | workers | *nameless
exam: Which sentence uses nameless to mean a feeling too strange to describe? | The nameless stranger wore a red coat | The nameless letter arrived on Monday | The nameless boy was called Sam | *She woke with a nameless fear she could not explain
